{"images":["data:image/webp;base64,"],"messages":[{"content":"A 53-year-old man suffers a cardiac arrest and his wife calls paramedics, who arrive a few minutes later and begin resuscitative measures. A regular heart rate is established after about 40 minutes of resuscitative efforts as he is being transported to the hospital. A thrombolytic agent is administered on admission. Which of the following cellular changes is most likely to now be occurring within his myocardium? <image> \n\n(A) Apoptosis\n(B) Free radical injury\n(C) Heterophagocytosis\n(D) Squamous metaplasia\n\nAnswer with the option's letter from the given choices directly.","role":"user"}]}